   ***  tAo  PARAMETERS FILE  ***
	(default unities : I.S.)


PARAMETER VALUES			CORRESPONDING VARIABLES			USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Gridding:
501 	201				nx	nz				(Number of x (distance) and z (depth for rheological calculations))

Limits:
0	1e6				x0	xf				(modelizated x range)

Graphic & file output window:
0	1e6	-4000	2000		xmin   xmax     ymin   ymax		(limits of the output window)

Lithosph. geometry:
20000	32000	15000			espelast, espcort, espcortsup 		(default ET (if no .EET file) ; default crustal geometry for gravity anomaly and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST)
0	0				altmedidaanom (0 for Bouguer anomaly)	alt0 (altitude of  the initial plate position from sea level)

Densities:
2900	3300	0	2800	2300	dens(corteza,manto,amb,infill,sedims)	(densities of crust (just for anomaly calculation), mantle, air (water for oceanic flexure), infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1), sediments)

Erosion model parameters:
0e1	-0e-15	.0	1e2		Kerosdif, Keroseol, Ksedim, maxprofsed	(constants of:  diffusive erosion, continental background erosion rate, water sedimentation and  max. water thickness contributing to sedimentation)

Restoring force constant. Zero means default=g·(densmanto-densamb) :
0					Krest					(restoring force constant)

Time to be elapsed between consecutive recorded horizons:
0					dtmemohori				(time between two consecutives horizons)

Time variables:
0	0	1	.1		Time(ini, final, tau, dt)		(initial, final, relaxation and viscoelastic-step   times in Ma)

Boundary Conditions:
3					boundary_conds				(0: Continuous simetric half-plate. 1: Broken plate.  2: Continuous plate,  3: Free ends,  4: Hunging plate)

External forces:
0e12	0e12	0e17			tecforce, appshearforce, appmoment 	(Horizontal tectonic force, applied force and torque as bound. cond. case 1. (left side))

These are switches to turn on options of the model.
Their possible values are 1 (yes) or 0 (no):
0	0	0			switch_(visc, rheolimit, topoest)	(switches for: viscoelastic model, rheological calculation, load to stay without moving)
0	0	0			switch_(erosed,compactar,mar)		(switches for: erosional-deositional model, compacting(not available),  existence of sea)
0	1	0	1		switch_(calcanom,output,writeps,writefile)(switches for:  calculate gravity anomaly, file output, postscript output(PV-WAVE), graphic output(PV-WAVE))
0	0				switch_(verbose, debug)			(switches for: more runtime prints)

v3.1					release


(END OF PARAMETERS FILE)
Comments:
  This is a tAo 3.1 parameter file. You can run the simplest model (without any load file
  *.CRG) just varying the b.c. parameters 'appshearforce' & 'appmoment' and the 'tecforce'
  external horizontal force. 
	Default unities: I.S.  (except indication).
	If  (Krest != 0)  then the restoring force wouldn't be that of the Arquimedes (lithos. 
		over liquid mantle) but this given value.
	If  (avistopoest != 0) then the load will rest at zero level and plate subsidence will 
		be filled with 'densinfill' material. Do not use with erosion model.
	'tecforce' is compressive if >0.